      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T11:56:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit:\nIIUC the idea is to have AutomaticOnOffKeepaliveTracker wrap KeepaliveTracker to do the auto on-off; and KeepaliveTracker shouldn\u0027t need to care about on-off behavior. AutomaticOnOffKeepaliveTracker is the class that controls the global start/stop state now.\n\nPassing down automaticOnOffKeepalives to KeepaliveTracker kind of breaks this design. And it\u0027s also weird if you consider that it\u0027s only used to build a message to ConnectivityService to be sent back to this AutomaticOnOffKeepaliveTracker.\n\nActually it looks like KeepaliveTracker.startNattKeepalive could just be `KeepaliveInfo makeNattKeepaliveInfo` now (could even be static with a few adjustments to KeepaliveInfo to make it static), as I think it doesn\u0027t change any state, it just builds a KeepaliveInfo to be sent to ConnectivityService.\n\nThen you could move mConnectivityServiceHandler.obtainMessage(...).sendToTarget() here, which I think would look better as it\u0027s AutomaticOnOffKeepaliveTracker\u0027s job to manage when CMD_START_SOCKET_KEEPALIVE gets sent (it also does it in handleMaybeResumeKeepalive).\n\nCould be refactored in another CL if that makes sense",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 416,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 416,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "69f2f2d556b940473611d091a1881304989dee86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
